/// `thir`: its two texts name a Rust file beside the source and a function of
/// that file, whose staged THIR is the signature's value. The dispatcher stages
/// a mark only when its texts hold no escape. This file holds one, so the mark
/// has no staged answer, with a reader and with none.
@[refuses("StagedBody.Unanswered")]
@[thir(("example\t.rs", "identity"))]
def identityBody : Integer;
